(2978680, 413603, 64918, '<td valign="top"><i>Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest...</i> <br/>Love the cloud formation - esp the angry looking cloud centre top which gives the composition a sense of movement... kinda feels lacking in dynamics though -  a flat and unexciting foreground with nothing happening on the skyline.<br/>Also don''t get a feel for ''after the game'' - there''s some kind of netting structure there but I can''t figure what it is (though if it''s something like baseball or the like it might be more obvious to an American viewer - so I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt on that). :)</td>', 'Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest... Love the cloud formation - esp the angry looking cloud centre top which gives the composition a sense of movement... kinda feels lacking in dynamics though -  a flat and unexciting foreground with nothing happening on the skyline.Also don''t get a feel for ''after the game'' - there''s some kind of netting structure there but I can''t figure what it is (though if it''s something like baseball or the like it might be more obvious to an American viewer - so I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt on that). :)', '2006-10-31 12:25:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2978793, 414589, 64918, '<td valign="top"><i>Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest...</i> <br/>Would have liked more light/highlights evident in the main row of seats but the  receeding seats work very well in drawing the eye into the image.<br/>Maybe an empty paper cup in one of the cup holders just to add a point of interest/contrast to the scene?</td>', 'Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest... Would have liked more light/highlights evident in the main row of seats but the  receeding seats work very well in drawing the eye into the image.Maybe an empty paper cup in one of the cup holders just to add a point of interest/contrast to the scene?', '2006-10-31 13:11:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2978812, 416108, 64918, '<td valign="top"><i>Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest...</i> <br/>Kinda doesn''t meet the challenge for me... without the title there''d be no indication that a sporting event had taken place... as it''s a victory celebration maybe you could have included a trophy of some kind within the image.. or a baseball glove etc.(?)</td>', 'Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest... Kinda doesn''t meet the challenge for me... without the title there''d be no indication that a sporting event had taken place... as it''s a victory celebration maybe you could have included a trophy of some kind within the image.. or a baseball glove etc.(?)', '2006-10-31 13:19:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2978813, 416785, 64918, '<td valign="top"><i>Just my opinions - take what''s useful, bin the rest...</i> <br/>Composition feels weak - 50/50 split of land/sky feels static... greater use of the rope barrier (ie get in MUCH closer and a lower PoV) could have helped lead the eye into the image more....<br/>Also can''t find any point of focus here - and the lighting is very flat.<br/>On the plus side - those clouds are really dramatic really ominous feeling - maybe you could have made them more of a feature of the overall image.<br/>I''d suggest getting in closer and looking for more dramatic/dynamic angles.</td>', 'Just my opinions - take what''s useful, bin the rest... Composition feels weak - 50/50 split of land/sky feels static... greater use of the rope barrier (ie get in MUCH closer and a lower PoV) could have helped lead the eye into the image more....Also can''t find any point of focus here - and the lighting is very flat.On the plus side - those clouds are really dramatic really ominous feeling - maybe you could have made them more of a feature of the overall image.I''d suggest getting in closer and looking for more dramatic/dynamic angles.', '2006-10-31 13:19:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2978824, 415416, 64918, '<td valign="top"><i>Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest...</i> <br/>Bit of a literal interpretation, in the sense I don''t feel any emotion here... maybe that was your point, end of the game and all the emotion has drained out.<br/>The composition widthwise feels good - the structure is nicely balanced and the eye flows around the stadium - I''d consider cropping  up from the bottom about 50% of the shadow area though - it''s kinda dead space and it''s draining the impact of the structure for me.</td>', 'Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest... Bit of a literal interpretation, in the sense I don''t feel any emotion here... maybe that was your point, end of the game and all the emotion has drained out.The composition widthwise feels good - the structure is nicely balanced and the eye flows around the stadium - I''d consider cropping  up from the bottom about 50% of the shadow area though - it''s kinda dead space and it''s draining the impact of the structure for me.', '2006-10-31 13:26:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2978829, 414090, 64918, '<td valign="top"><i>Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest...</i> <br/>Would praying not be a pre-match rather than post-match activity? Well, I''m a Brit and I''m not sure about the protocol here - so I''ll give you the benfit of the doubt on that one. :)<br/>I like the crop taking out part of his boot - just saying that ''cos I''m guessing you may get picked up on it by others. I''m not saying they''re wrong but for me it adds to the off-centred feel and gives it a bit of edge somehow.<br/>Think I might consider a slight crop from the bottom just to remove the white line bottom right (distracting once you''ve spotted it).<br/>Not sure what the partial saturation achieves here - for me it takes away from the overall mood of the image since I notice the team logo more than the activity of the player.<br/>Nice exposure and the patterns in the grass work well in directing attention towards the players bowed head.</td>', 'Just my observations - take what you need and bin the rest... Would praying not be a pre-match rather than post-match activity? Well, I''m a Brit and I''m not sure about the protocol here - so I''ll give you the benfit of the doubt on that one. :)I like the crop taking out part of his boot - just saying that ''cos I''m guessing you may get picked up on it by others. I''m not saying they''re wrong but for me it adds to the off-centred feel and gives it a bit of edge somehow.Think I might consider a slight crop from the bottom just to remove the white line bottom right (distracting once you''ve spotted it).Not sure what the partial saturation achieves here - for me it takes away from the overall mood of the image since I notice the team logo more than the activity of the player.Nice exposure and the patterns in the grass work well in directing attention towards the players bowed head.', '2006-10-31 13:28:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2978844, 416129, 3102, '<td valign="top">My favorite of the bunch.  I have shots like this from inside a stadium that I would have loved to have entered, but naturally the timing of the challenge wasn''t right :)</td>', 'My favorite of the bunch.  I have shots like this from inside a stadium that I would have loved to have entered, but naturally the timing of the challenge wasn''t right :)', '2006-10-31 13:37:21.000000', NULL, 1),
